chore dep updat modul github com charmbracelet x ansi to v0 10 2 by renov bot in http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go pull 7432 chore dep updat golang org x telemetri digest to 8e64475 by renov bot in http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go pull 7431 chore dep updat ossf scorecard action action to v2 43 by renov bot in http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go pull 7435 allow optim lock for built in exemplar reservoir by dashpol in http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go pull 7423\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8765f6c08a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/releases/release-v1.39.0.md\", \"id\": \"3d17045ae4a36b55\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.42979646878848904, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.2411877239835558, \"vector_similarity\": 0.86988354, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/releases/release-v1.39.0.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8765f6c08a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/releases/release-v1.39.0.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/releases/release-v1.39.0.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 52878, \"chunk_count\": 30, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:09:56\", \"token_count\": 15994, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-04]\\n\\n# Pull Request: Use sync.Map and atomics to improve sum performance (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go#7427)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/pull/7427  \\n\\n**Author**: dashpole  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-09-29T14:36:56Z · **Updated**: 2025-10-14T14:40:27Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: merged (2025-10-07T13:40:23Z)  \\n\\n**Branch**: `optimize_counter_syncmap` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +437 / -121 across 14 files  \\n\\n**Labels**: area:metrics  \\n\\n**Milestone**: v1.39.0\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nAlternative to https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/pull/7380\\n\\nThis uses a sync.Map and atomics for the sum's counter value.  This intentionally introduces a new race condition that didn't previously exist:\\n\\n* It is possible for the exemplar to be recorded in the batch of metrics after the add() for cumulative sum aggregations. For cumulative, this isn't a huge issue since exemplars are expected to persist across collection cycles. This is difficult to fix because we can't manage the internal storage of an exemplar.Reservoir (to atomically swap between hot and cold storage).  If we are able to make assumptions about how exemplar reservoirs are managed (i.e. that the number of and order of exemplars returned is always the same), then we could possibly fix this by merging at export time.\\n\\n### Alternatives Considered\\n\\n#### RWLock for the map instead of sync.Map\\n\\nThis is significantly less performant.\\n\\n#### Single sync.Map without hotColdWaitGroup\\n\\nDeleting keys from the sync.Map concurrently with measurements (during Clear() of the sync.Map) can cause measurements to be made to a counter that has already been read, exported and deleted.  This can produce incorrect sums when delta is used.  Instead, atomically switching writes to a completely empty sync.Map and waiting for writes to the previous sync.Map complete eliminates this issue.\\n\\n#### Use two sync.Map for cumulative sums\\n\\nOne idea I explored was doing a hot-cold swap for cumulative sums just like we do for delta sums.  We would swap the hot and cold sync.Maps, wait for writes to the cold sync.Map to complete while new writes go to the hot map.  Then, once we are done reading the cold map, we could merge the contents of the cold map back into the new hot map.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src pr 04 pull request use sync map and atom to improv sum perform open telemetri opentelemetri go 7427 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go pull 7427 author dashpol creat 2025 09 29t14 36 56z updat 2025 10 14t14 40 27z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state merg 2025 10 07t13 40 23z branch optim _ counter _ syncmap main chang 437 121 across 14 file label area metric mileston v1 39 0 descript altern to http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go pull 7380 this us a sync map and atom for the sum s counter valu this intent introduc a new race condit that didn t previous exist it is possibl for the exemplar to be record in the batch of metric after the add for cumul sum aggreg for cumul this isn t a huge issu sinc exemplar are expect to persist across collect cycl this is difficult to fix becaus we can t manag the intern storag of an exemplar reservoir to atom swap between hot and cold storag if we are abl to make assumpt about how exemplar reservoir are manag i e that the number of and order of exemplar return is alway the same then we could possibl fix this by merg at export time altern consid rwlock for the map instead of sync map this is signific less perform singl sync map without hotcoldwaitgroup delet key from the sync map concurr with measur dure clear of the sync map can caus measur to be made to a counter that ha alreadi been read export and delet this can produc incorrect sum when delta is use instead atom switch write to a complet empti sync map and wait for write to the previous sync map complet elimin this issu use two sync map for cumul sum one idea i explor wa do a hot cold swap for cumul sum just like we do for delta sum we would swap the hot and cold sync map wait for write to the cold sync map to complet while new write go to the hot map then onc we are done read the cold map we could merg the content of the cold map back into the new hot map\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \